WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:04.820
Well, it was bound to happen eventually: the
Rise of Skywalker rumor mill has finally churned

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:06.240
out a genuine gut punch.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:10.599
Reddit user JediPaxis, who claims to be close
to the film's production, has been busily

00:00:10.599 --> 00:00:14.619
leaking what they claim to be the entire plot
of the film over the last month or so.

00:00:14.619 --> 00:00:19.150
Their latest revelation has to do with C-3PO,
and, if it's got any truth to it, it seems

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:22.380
that more than a few fans' hearts are going
to be broken into pieces.

00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:26.080
Of course, it's important to point out that
this report has been in no way confirmed.

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:29.911
The rumors around The Rise of Skywalker have
been flying fast and furious of late, and

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:34.040
nothing substantial has come from any official
sources that back up JediPaxis' leaks.

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:38.860
That said, the reports offered up by JediPaxis
carry an air of legitimacy for one compelling

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:42.329
reason: several of the plot points which they
have put forward have been verified by Star

00:00:42.329 --> 00:00:45.420
Wars fan sites, who each cite their own independent
sources.

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:50.540
Bespin Bulletin and Jason Ward of MakingStarWars.com
have both corroborated specific elements of

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:54.250
JediPaxis' reports — so there's a good chance
some of these leaks contain at least some

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:55.240
accurate information.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:58.800
It should also be mentioned that The Rise
of Skywalker is currently in the midst of

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:02.300
reshoots, so some of the plot details that
are being reported on at this time could easily

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:04.660
change by the time the final cut hits theaters.

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:09.420
Having said all of that, do be aware: potentially
huge spoilers for The Rise of Skywalker lay

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:09.920
ahead.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:14.440
This particular rumor revolves around a mysterious
dagger which was once owned by a Force user

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:18.800
loyal to the Sith, and upon it is inscribed
a message in an unidentifiable language.

00:01:18.860 --> 00:01:22.840
During the course of the film, Rey, Poe, and
Finn are led to believe that this dagger may

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:27.030
be the key to locating a Wayfinder, a device
that for plot reasons is desperately sought

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:29.420
after by both the movie's heroes and villains.

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:32.340
Putting a long story short: it has a lot to
do with this guy right here.

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:37.020
Luckily, the heroes are able to locate the
dagger, but C-3PO despite being fluent in

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:41.280
over six million forms of communication can
only identify the inscription as an ancient

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:45.520
Sith language, one which he cannot translate
due to restrictions in his programming.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:49.280
Finn, Rey and Poe subsequently enlist the
aid of an old acquaintance of Poe's named

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:53.580
Zorri Bliss to track down someone capable
of hacking the protocol droid's programming,

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:55.440
thus allowing him to provide a translation.

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:57.590
They're able to do so, but there's a catch.

00:01:57.820 --> 00:01:59.760
And it's a pretty significant catch, too.

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:03.900
Zorri's contact informs Rey, Poe, and Finn
that he can get them what they want but if

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:06.720
he does, C-3PO's memory will be completely
wiped.

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:10.700
Understandably, the heroes are reluctant to
lose their faithful companion, but this is

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:13.560
where C-3PO finally gets his moment in the
spotlight.

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:17.840
The droid insists that the procedure be carried
out, knowing full well that, for all intents

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:19.700
and purposes, it will lead to his death.

00:02:19.849 --> 00:02:24.980
Zorri's contact does his thing, and the modification
results in a new, red-eyed look for 3PO, as

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:27.960
seen in the D23 trailer that debuted earlier
this year.

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:31.940
The droid is then able to read the dagger's
inscription, which reveals the location of

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:32.660
the Wayfinder.

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:37.700
Once his task is complete, C-3PO reboots — and
after that happens, he's no longer the droid

00:02:37.709 --> 00:02:40.600
he once was, instead now little more than
a blank slate.

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:45.090
It's worth noting that C-3PO has appeared
in every single Star Wars film save for Solo:

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:46.120
A Star Wars Story.

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:49.820
It's also safe to say that he's been more
prone to cowardice than heroism during that

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:50.320
time.

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:53.900
But if The Rise of Skywalker is to be the
character's last on-screen appearance, which

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:58.569
it almost certainly is, it seems apt to finally
give this iconic protocol droid a genuine

00:02:58.569 --> 00:02:59.819
moment of heroic self-sacrifice.

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:02.780
"I never knew I had it in me."

